    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">A number is called a Mirror Number if:<br><br>- Reversing its digits produces a number different from the original.<br>- The sum of the original number and its reversed number is a palindrome.<br><br>Determine whether <var>N</var> is a Mirror Number.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\">A positive integer <var>N</var>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\">If <var>N</var> is a Mirror Number: <const>Yes, <var>N</var> is a Mirror Number</const><br><br>If <var>N</var> is a palindrome: <const>No, <var>N</var> is a Palindrome</const><br><br>Otherwise: <const>No, M is not a Palindrome</const><br><br>where <var>M</var> is the sum of <var>N</var> and its reversed number.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; <var>N</var> &le; 1000</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">56</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">Yes, 56 is a Mirror Number</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
